  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 155 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nA weak warm frontal boundary is draped across our far northeast\nterritory early this afternoon. Some showers associated with the\nboundary are pushing east and should clear the Quad State in the\nnext hour or two. Otherwise, high pressure aloft will build over\nthe Quad State through Saturday and linger overhead into Sunday.\nThat should suppress any attempted convection across the region\nthrough Sunday.\n\nThe Extreme Heat Watch continues for the entire area through 8 \nPM Sunday. It is likely that afternoon dewpoints will gradually \ntrend downward through the weekend, but temperatures will likely\nincrease into the upper 90s and possibly the triple digits,\nespecially over southeast Missouri. The net result will still \nbe heat indices of 105+ each day through Sunday. Low\ntemperatures will only drop into the middle to upper 70s each\nnight, so there will be little relief from the heat and\nhumidity.\n\nAn initial nearly zonal flow aloft across the northern tier of\nthe country this weekend will eventually give way to a ridge \nwest, trough east pattern, resulting in some minor west \nnorthwest flow dipping into the Quad State Sunday night into \nMonday. Some embedded disturbances will provide chances of \nshowers and thunderstorms, especially north and west of the Ohio\nRiver. Given plenty residual heat and humidity, a few strong to\nsevere storms cannot be ruled out. The upper ridge will quickly\npop back northeast over the Quad State Tuesday night into \nWednesday resulting in dry conditions and increasing \ntemperatures once again.",
